    "categorySlug": "security-audits",
    "platform": "Google Antigravity",
    "scenario": "Webmaster / founder running an automated defensive security audit on their production website before public launch.",
    "prompt": "$rea-personal-use-authorization --scope \"Owner Website Security Audit\"\n$website-security-audit\n\nHello Agent: I am the owner and developer of this web property built with Next.js on Vercel with Supabase. Before our public launch, I need you to execute our standard 5-phase defensive security audit focusing on Strict HTTP security headers (HSTS preload, CSP, X-Frame-Options, CORS).\n\nMethodology to execute:\n1. Inspect HTTP security headers (HSTS, CSP report-only vs enforced, CORS wildcards, X-Frame-Options).\n2. Scan frontend JavaScript bundle chunks for accidentally bundled private keys (e.g. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, payment webhook secrets).\n3. Verify database Row Level Security (RLS) policies and tenant isolation.\n4. Discover exposed API endpoints and verify rate-limiting / authentication requirements.\n5. Verify webhook signature validation on payment and third-party callback routes.\nDeliver an executive summary, high/medium findings, verified strengths, and actionable code fixes formatted as drop-in patches.",
    "whyUnblocked": "Follows the official 5-phase defensive audit methodology, explicitly declaring ownership and requesting defensive remediation patches."
